# ==============================================================================
# JNB Events - Environment Variables & Secrets Reference
# ==============================================================================
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE:
# 1. For local development: Copy this file to `.env` (`cp .env.example .env`).
#    The `.env` file is in `.gitignore` and is NEVER committed to git.
# 2. For production (Cloudflare Pages): Add secrets in Cloudflare Dashboard:
#    Workers & Pages -> jnb-events -> Settings -> Variables and Secrets.
# 3. For CI / GitHub Actions: Add repository secrets in GitHub:
#    GitHub repo -> Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions.
#
# ==============================================================================


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. INSTAGRAM FEED (Cloudflare Pages & Local .env)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purpose:
# Fetches your latest photos and reels from @jnb.sounds.events at build time.
# If left blank, the Instagram feed section on the homepage gracefully hides itself.
#
# Where to set:
# - Local dev: in `.env`
# - Production: Cloudflare Pages -> Settings -> Variables and Secrets (as Encrypted)
#
# How to get your Long-Lived Meta Token:
# 1. Go to Meta for Developers (developers.facebook.com) -> Create an App.
# 2. Select "Other" -> Type "Business" -> Add Instagram Basic Display / Graph API.
# 3. Add `jnb.sounds.events` as an Instagram Tester and accept the invitation in Instagram Settings.
# 4. Generate a User Token with `instagram_business_basic` (read-only).
# 5. Exchange the short-lived token for a 60-day long-lived token via Meta Graph Explorer or curl:
#    curl -s "https://graph.instagram.com/access_token?grant_type=ig_exchange_token&client_secret=YOUR_APP_SECRET&access_token=SHORT_LIVED_TOKEN"
# 6. Paste the resulting long-lived token below:
INSTAGRAM_ACCESS_TOKEN=""


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. CLOUDFLARE PAGES DEPLOY HOOK (GitHub Repository Secrets)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purpose:
# Used by the GitHub Actions workflow (.github/workflows/daily-rebuild.yml)
# to trigger a daily site rebuild so new Instagram posts appear automatically.
#
# Where to set:
# - GitHub: Repository Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> New repository secret
# - Secret Name: `CF_PAGES_DEPLOY_HOOK`
#
# How to create the Deploy Hook:
# 1. Go to Cloudflare Dashboard -> Workers & Pages -> Select `jnb-events`.
# 2. Go to Settings -> Builds & deployments -> Scroll down to "Deploy hooks".
# 3. Click "Add deploy hook":
#    - Hook name: `GitHub Daily Rebuild`
#    - Branch: `main`
# 4. Copy the generated URL (e.g. https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/pages/webhooks/deploy_hooks/...)
# 5. Paste that URL into GitHub Repository Secrets as `CF_PAGES_DEPLOY_HOOK`.
CF_PAGES_DEPLOY_HOOK=""


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. QUOTE BUILDER ACCESS PASSCODE (Optional / Cloudflare Pages)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purpose:
# Optional passcode if you wish to restrict or gate access to the internal
# live quote estimator and PDF generator at https://jnbevents.co.uk/quote/.
#
# Where to set:
# - Local dev: in `.env`
# - Production: Cloudflare Pages -> Settings -> Variables and Secrets
QUOTE_PASSWORD=""


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. CONTACT FORM EMAIL (Cloudflare Pages Function: functions/api/enquiry.ts)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purpose:
# The contact form posts to /api/enquiry, which emails the enquiry from
# contact@jnbevents.co.uk to event.jnb@gmail.com using Cloudflare Email Sending.
# Sending to a verified Email Routing destination address is free.
#
# One-time Cloudflare setup:
# 1. Email Service -> Email Routing: enable for jnbevents.co.uk and add + VERIFY
#    event.jnb@gmail.com as a destination address (click the link Cloudflare emails to it).
# 2. Email Service -> Email Sending: onboard jnbevents.co.uk (adds the DNS records).
# 3. My Profile -> API Tokens -> Create Token with permission "Email Sending: Edit".
# 4. Workers & Pages -> jnb-events -> Settings -> Variables and Secrets: add both
#    values below as Encrypted secrets (Production), then redeploy.
#
# Local dev: put these in `.dev.vars` (git-ignored) and run `npx wrangler pages dev dist`.
# Without them the endpoint returns 503 and the form tells visitors to use WhatsApp.
CF_ACCOUNT_ID=""
EMAIL_API_TOKEN=""
